# why: Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf) would turn LF into CRLF; scripts, fixtures and hashes expect the files
# exactly as committed, so text stays LF everywhere and binary documents are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf
# PowerShell scripts in Windows style (Notepad, PowerShell ISE)
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
